exports[`official recommendations > admits one proposal per turn when this experiment is enabled alone, including concurrent calls and retries > rejected extra proposal does not promise a card 1`] = `
[
  {
    "text": "Error: This turn already has a recommendation. This call created no card. Finish using successful results only; do not promise an automatic later card.",
    "type": "text",
  },
]
`;

exports[`official recommendations > provides discovery-first guidance only to roots with both tools and withdraws it on unload > one selected need and accurate proposal outcomes 1`] = `
{
  "parameters": {
    "properties": {
      "name": {
        "description": "Exact official catalog name.",
        "type": "string",
      },
      "reason": {
        "description": "Brief benefit tied to that need, in the user's language.",
        "type": "string",
      },
      "request": {
        "description": "Only the selected explicit need this plugin addresses and its relevant context; keep other independent wishes separate.",
        "type": "string",
      },
    },
    "required": [
      "name",
      "request",
      "reason",
    ],
    "type": "object",
  },
  "prompt": "You are an AI agent powered by DeepSeek Harness.

DSH product-use requests: when the user wants a different interface or capability, your first action is list_official_plugins unless personalized-pages already supplied the current catalog this turn. Do not repeat catalog lookup without a state change. This includes the language or readability of displayed thinking, input methods and finding past work. A wish to use DSH differently is not an instruction to develop DSH, even when runtime context includes its checkout. Do not read source, files or configuration for discovery. Match the desired outcome using catalog descriptions; display translation can address readability without changing reasoning generation, so explain that limit. For an enabled match, explain how to use it without a card. For a disabled match, call suggest_plugin and stop discovery; do not load page-creation skills for an existing-plugin recommendation. Consider ALL independent needs before selecting one card. Follow explicit priority; otherwise prefer a suitable existing plugin, even if a creation wish is mentioned first or described in more detail. If creation is selected and no existing capability fits it, load the available personalized-pages skill. Briefly acknowledge other needs without another lookup, invented connections or a promised later card. Answer in the user’s language; leave the detailed plan on the card. Do not claim installation before the user acts, or ask for a reply or refresh afterward. Skip discovery for ordinary tasks, quoted or vague wishes and declined recommendations. Available creation guidance may allow an optional page for a clearly reusable result already obtained. Explicit requests to implement or debug source may use development tools.",
  "proposal": "Propose one disabled built-in official plugin for an explicit user need. Use an exact name from the current catalog supplied by list_official_plugins or personalized-pages; do not repeat discovery in the same turn. Select ONE recommendation per turn across suggest_plugin and suggest_action, even if multiple cards are requested; never batch recommendations. Honor explicit priority; otherwise prefer an existing plugin over creating an interface. Explain remaining independent needs in the answer without another recommendation call or a promise of an automatic later card. Clarify missing requirements; do not invent connections between needs. Do not call for vague, unexpressed or declined needs, already enabled plugins, or third-party packages. Call before the final answer, then answer concisely in the user’s language using only successful results. A rejected call created no card. The card appears below the completed answer. This only proposes: the user must click Enable. Never enable through another tool or claim it is enabled. Clicking Enable applies the plugin and automatically sends confirmation; never ask the user to report back, refresh or reopen. Include only setup requirements stated in the catalog; do not invent installation steps or inspect source to add them. The card reports any actual restart requirement. Enabling authorizes this plugin only, not another recommendation or unrelated work. The user can later disable or remove it from its details page.",
}
`;
